# AMD64 thunk export spec -- wldap32.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Boltgun imports this module STATICALLY and
# it had no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module
# (c000007b) and the whole image failed to load (c0000135).
#
# Boltgun imports it BY ORDINAL AND ONLY BY ORDINAL -- sixteen numbers, no
# names, which is exactly the class of request the ordinal work of 2026-08-17
# made answerable at all.  Measured, with the names Wine's own wldap32.spec
# gives those numbers:
#
#   143 ldap_init          46 ldap_unbind_s       211 ldap_set_option
#    60 ldap_simple_bind_s 50 ldap_search_s        41 ldap_msgfree
#    22 ldap_err2string   200 ldap_memfree         26 ldap_first_entry
#    27 ldap_next_entry    32 ldap_first_attribute 33 ldap_next_attribute
#    35 ldap_get_values_len 79 ldap_value_free_len 30 ldap_get_dn
#   301 ber_free
DLL wldap32.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# winldap.h is not in the oracle's default translation unit; without it every
# one of the 244 eligible exports was refused.
#
# winldap.h renames its ANSI/Unicode pairs too -- ldap_initA (line 535) /
# ldap_initW (536) are declared directly, and the undecorated ldap_init is
# only `#define ldap_init WINELIB_NAME_AW(ldap_init)`, ~120 siblings the
# same way -- which LOOKS like psapi.dll's PSAPI_VERSION rename (see
# dlls/psapi/psapi.thunks): the oracle resolves an export NAME, and a header
# is entitled to declare that name's implementation under another one.
#
# It does NOT take the same PROBE-DEFINE treatment, though, because it is a
# different mechanism: WINELIB_NAME_AW is keyed on UNICODE (a per-CALL-SITE
# switch every Winelib header uses this same way, not a module-local
# version knob), and no single -D flag makes it declare ldap_init itself.
# What actually resolves it is wldap32.spec's OWN alias column -- every
# renamed line already names its target directly, e.g.
# `143 cdecl ldap_init(str long) ldap_initA` -- and spec2thunk's oracle
# already retries a "no declaration found" export under that .spec-named
# alias (see the exception handler in resolve_signatures() keyed on
# e['spec_alias']).  That mechanism did not exist when this file's ordinal
# table above was first measured; it does now, and it needs no help from
# this file.
#
# Measured today: 244 eligible, 230 emitted, 14 refused.  Of Boltgun's
# sixteen ordinals, fifteen are served (including all ten this file used to
# name as still-refused).  The lone holdout is ber_free (301), and NOT for
# an A/W reason -- winber.h declares it (and ber_alloc_t/ber_init/
# ber_bvecfree/ber_bvdup/ber_skip_tag/ber_peek_tag/ber_first_element/
# ber_next_element/ber_flatten/ber_printf/ber_scanf) under its own plain
# name with no rename at all; this file simply does not PROBE-EXTRA that
# header.  (ldap_next_reference and ldap_set_dbg_flags are also still
# refused, declared in no Wine header under any name -- a different, older,
# and unrelated gap.)  None of this is in scope for the psapi PROBE-DEFINE
# fix; left as found.
PROBE-EXTRA   winldap.h

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 2026-08-30 Civilization VI triage: ordinal 301, ber_free
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EOSSDK-Win64-Shipping.dll imports WLDAP32 ordinal 301 BY ORDINAL -- the one
# number in the sixteen listed above that FROM-SPEC auto still refused, as
# "no declaration found in Wine headers".  The comment above is right that
# winldap.h is the missing header for the ldap_* family, but ber_free is not
# in winldap.h at all: it is declared in include/winber.h:29,
#
#     void CDECL ber_free( BerElement *, int );
#
# a flat prototype the oracle can read.  Its siblings (ber_alloc_t, ber_init,
# ber_bvfree, ber_first_element, ber_next_element, ber_peek_tag, ber_scanf,
# ber_printf, ber_flatten) come along with the same one line, which is worth
# having: an application that walks a BER element uses several of them and
# would otherwise take a sentinel on the second call instead of the first.
PROBE-EXTRA winber.h
